        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/09/03/apple-watch-loses-a-useful-multitasking-feature-in-watchos-27-that-ive-been-missing/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/apple-watch-ultra-modular-face.webp?w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">I mentioned today in <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/09/03/we-need-to-talk-about-siri-ai-for-apple-watch/\">my Siri AI Apple Watch piece</a> that there’s one change I still hope Apple makes to watchOS 27 before it ships this month. It’s one of those common muscle-memory features that have existed for years, and I’ve been missing it all summer.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"apple-watch,watchos,watchos-27\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1067294\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/09/03/apple-watch-loses-a-useful-multitasking-feature-in-watchos-27-that-ive-been-missing/#more-1067294\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
        "type": "Technology",
