        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2024/05/m4-ipad-pro-hero-image.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Last year, Apple completely <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2025/06/18/these-ipados-26-features-make-the-ipad-more-mac-like-than-ever/\">reinvented multitasking</a> on the iPad, with the introduction of windowing in iPadOS 26. At first, this meant the removal of the simpler version of multitasking, Split View and Slide Over. Those features did <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2025/10/06/ipados-26-1-beta-2-restores-slide-over-multitasking-back-to-ipad/\">eventually return</a>, but at a cost – they required you to use the clunky new windowing system. I was hoping iPadOS 27 would improve this, but it didn’t.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"ipados-27,opinion\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1060453\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/09/05/ipados-27-still-needs-simpler-multitasking-heres-what-id-like-to-see/#more-1060453\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
