        "title": "watchOS 27 removes three features that Apple Watch users might miss after updating",
        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/09/04/watchos-27-removes-three-features-that-apple-watch-users-might-miss-after-updating/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/09/siri-ai-apple-watch-1.webp?w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">When watchOS 27 is released later this month, Apple Watch users may notice that some things work a bit differently. The upcoming software update removes three features that users may miss after updating.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"apple-watch,watchos,watchos-27\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1067445\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/09/04/watchos-27-removes-three-features-that-apple-watch-users-might-miss-after-updating/#more-1067445\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
