        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/09/01/new-apple-ceo-john-ternus-now-has-his-own-x-account/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/09/john-ternus-joins-twitter.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The new Apple CEO has just launched their social media presence on X, with the handle <a href=\"https://x.com/johnternus\">@johnternus</a>. His bio is simply ‘ CEO’, and his first post simply reads ‘hello’.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Today is Ternus’s first official day in the top job, with outgoing Tim Cook <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/09/01/apple-leadership-page-updated-as-john-ternus-becomes-the-new-ceo/\">moving to an Executive Chair role</a>.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"aapl\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1066948\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/09/01/new-apple-ceo-john-ternus-now-has-his-own-x-account/#more-1066948\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
