        "title": "Apple making just a few hundred iPhone Ultras per day, per report",
        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/09/04/apple-making-just-a-few-hundred-iphone-ultras-per-day-per-report/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/07/iphone-ultra-concept-blue.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">We’re less than a week away from Apple announcing its first-ever foldable iPhone. A new supply chain report today says that Apple’s “extremely high quality control standards” have led to a much slower ramp for iPhone Ultra production so far.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"iphone,iphone-ultra\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1067364\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/09/04/apple-making-just-a-few-hundred-iphone-ultras-per-day-per-report/#more-1067364\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
